{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>For.</b> The hand of YHWH is His blow." "<b>And Moab shall be trampled.</b> For they came to help those who besieged Zion. ונדוש is a niphal from the binyanim that appear second [i.e., the passive stems], or from the doubled [pi'el/pu'al] stems." "<b>Like the trampling.</b> The noun [is] from the niphal binyan, and a shureq comes in place of a cholam, for they interchange." "<b>Madmenah.</b> The place of the madman."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:07.867440898Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}